# layered-name-collision root
library "X".

// A MULTI-LAYER library "X" that auto-splits into "X Concepts" / "X Asserted" /
// "X Inferred". The generated "X Asserted" name collides with the real sibling
// library "X Asserted" (x-asserted.crl), which root pulls into the emit closure
// via a qualified ref. The preflight must error with kind layered-name-collision.

terminology "VS":
- valueset is `vs`.

concept "Leaf":
- type is Observation.
- value type is CodeableConcept.
- coded from "VS".

// `Top` aliases the cross-library `X Asserted` boolean, which forces the `include XAsserted`
// this fixture asserts. (`Leaf` stays declared — it drives the RecordConcepts/RecordSource
// split — but is no longer composed into `Top`, whose former `sem-or` mixed a CodeableConcept
// operand into a boolean.)
concept "Top":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- defined as "X Asserted"."Sibling Concept".
